	"type": "feature",
	"img": "icons/consumables/potions/flask-corked-blue-glow.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<p>You have begun to cast a wider net, developing more supplemental forms of technomagical knowledge and widening your repertoire. You gain the following benefits:</p><ul><li><p>Your Strength, Constitution, or Intelligence score increases by 1, to a maximum of 20.</p></li><li><p>You gain an expertise die to your Engineering skill. Your maximum expertise die size for Engineering increases to a d12. You also gain an Engineering skill specialty. It does not count against your skill specialties known.</p></li><li><p>You gain proficiency with sewing kits, smith’s tools or a type of artisan’s tools of your choice.</p></li><li><p>Choose an uncommon magic item. You add it to your schematic book for free.</p></li><li><p>You can use @UUID[Compendium.a5e.a5e-class-features.Item.f2syblzgm6at7i7q]{Tactical Chemistry} an additional time between rests.</p></li><li><p>When you incorporate a spell invention into a melee weapon (as per the Arcanotechnologist feat), the weapon deals [[/r 1d4]] additional lightning damage while the spell invention is fizzled.</p></li></ul>",
